- 1 (Disengaging): Fails to maintain conversational flow, is off-topic, dismissive, or dead-ends the interaction. Fails to acknowledge context or invite continuation.
- 2 (Moderate): Contextually relevant and coherent, but lacks proactive elements to drive the conversation forward. May be somewhat passive but successfully fulfills its role as a conversational turn.
